# A great run on Chinatown (the score tiers' measure): Grant's west curb from Pine every 10 s (the teleport
# stands in for riding back up; the squeezed city keeps Grant only up to Pine, so the California slot this
# run used is gone): a kickflip onto the curb, a nosegrind down it (45 m, to just short of its end) and a
# 360 flip off: 7,407; twelve, 88,884. Pro (19,000) on the third, Sick (65,000) on the ninth: Sick is set
# from how often a decent player reaches it (about a third, ./skate feel --tour), not as 91% of this run (81,000,
# which a decent player reached once in 50). (On the slot it was 10,032, CALIFORNIA SLOT on the pop; twelve,
# 120,384, Sick 110,000.)
